{# bosun's changelog.

   The stock template renders `commit.message` — subject and body together —
   inside a single list item, with the commit link appended after it. A one-line
   commit survives that; anything longer does not: the body escapes the list,
   its headings collide with the version headings, and the link ends up orphaned
   far below the entry it belongs to. That matters here because merges are
   squashed with the pull request body as the commit body, so release entries
   are long by design.

   Three deliberate choices, each of which was wrong in an earlier draft:

   `commit.descriptions[0]` for the bullet. The parser puts the subject there
   with the `feat:`/`fix:` prefix already stripped, which is what you want when
   the type is the section heading directly above it.

   The RAW message for the body, not `descriptions[1:]`. Those are built by
   parse_paragraphs(), which does `paragraph.replace("\n", " ")` — it collapses
   single newlines into spaces, so markdown lists, tables and code fences come
   out as run-on text. Slicing the raw message keeps them intact.

   Headings in the body are demoted two levels. A release's own `##` heading
   renders as a sibling of the `## v1.2.3` version headings, so an expanded
   entry looks like it starts a new release. The rewrite is textual, so a line
   inside a fenced code block that begins with `##` would be demoted too — an
   acceptable trade for a document whose whole structure is versions.

   Escaping is handled in config, not here: `changelog.environment.autoescape`
   is true by default, which is right for HTML and wrong for markdown — it turns
   every apostrophe into `&#39;` and every quote into `&#34;`.
#}
{%- macro entry(commit) -%}
{%- set body = commit.message.partition("\n")[2] | trim -%}
* {{ commit.descriptions[0] | trim }} ([`{{ commit.short_hash }}`]({{ commit.hexsha | commit_hash_url }}))
{% if body %}
<details><summary>Details</summary>

{{ body | replace("\n#### ", "\n###### ") | replace("\n### ", "\n##### ") | replace("\n## ", "\n#### ") }}

</details>
{% endif %}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro section(heading, commits) -%}
### {{ heading | capitalize }}

{% for commit in commits %}{{ entry(commit) }}
{% endfor %}
{%- endmacro -%}
# CHANGELOG
{% if context.history.unreleased | length > 0 %}
## Unreleased

{% for type_, commits in context.history.unreleased | dictsort %}
{{ section(type_, commits) }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif -%}
{%- for version, release in context.history.released.items() %}
## {{ version.as_semver_tag() }} ({{ release.tagged_date.strftime("%Y-%m-%d") }})

{% for type_, commits in release["elements"] | dictsort %}
{{ section(type_, commits) }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endfor %}
